{% comment %}
  KRAMSAKON — variant swatches under a product card.

  For indigo textiles the variants are usually shades and patterns, so showing
  them on the card is genuinely useful: a customer sees the range without
  opening the product. It is also the one place a calm store can show breadth
  without resorting to badges or urgency (§2.2.3).

  Everything here is read from Shopify's NATIVE catalog — nothing is modelled
  in the theme. Two sources, in order of preference:

  1. Native swatches. If the owner has set swatch colours or swatch images on
     an option's values in the admin (Products → Options → the value's swatch),
     those are used. This is Shopify's built-in feature and the owner manages
     it entirely from the admin.
  2. Variant images. Otherwise, the distinct images across the product's
     variants are used as thumbnails. This needs no setup at all — assigning an
     image to a variant is ordinary catalog work.

  If neither exists, or the product has one variant, nothing renders.

  Accepts:
  - card_product: {Object} Product Liquid object. Required.
  - limit:        {Number} Max swatches before overflowing to "+N". Default 4.

  Usage:
    {% render 'kram-card-swatches', card_product: card_product %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign swatch_limit = limit | default: settings.kram_card_swatch_limit | default: 4

  comment
    Same detection idiom Dawn uses in snippets/product-variant-picker.liquid:
    an option qualifies when any of its values carries a swatch.
  endcomment
  assign swatch_option = null
  for option in card_product.options_with_values
    assign swatch_count = option.values | map: 'swatch' | compact | size
    if swatch_count > 0
      assign swatch_option = option
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if swatch_option -%}
  {%- comment -%} Source 1 — native option swatches {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign total = swatch_option.values.size
    assign overflow = total | minus: swatch_limit
  -%}
  <ul
    class="kram-card-swatches list-unstyled"
    role="list"
    aria-label="{{ 'kramsakon.product.available_options' | t: option: swatch_option.name }}"
  >
    {%- for value in swatch_option.values limit: swatch_limit -%}
      <li class="kram-card-swatches__item">
        <a
          href="{{ value.product_url | default: card_product.url }}"
          class="kram-card-swatches__link"
          aria-label="{{ card_product.title | escape }} — {{ value | escape }}"
        >
          {% render 'swatch', swatch: value.swatch, shape: 'square' %}
        </a>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if overflow > 0 -%}
      <li class="kram-card-swatches__more" aria-hidden="true">+{{ overflow }}</li>
    {%- endif -%}
  </ul>

{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Source 2 — distinct variant images.
    Variants often share one image, so collect distinct image ids first and
    count the true total before deciding what overflows. Without the
    de-duplication a product with 12 variants across 3 photographs would
    claim "+9" more choices than it has.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign seen_ids = ''
    assign distinct_total = 0
    for variant in card_product.variants
      if variant.image == blank
        continue
      endif
      assign key = variant.image.id | append: ','
      unless seen_ids contains key
        assign seen_ids = seen_ids | append: key
        assign distinct_total = distinct_total | plus: 1
      endunless
    endfor
    assign overflow = distinct_total | minus: swatch_limit
  -%}

  {%- if distinct_total > 1 -%}
    <ul class="kram-card-swatches list-unstyled" role="list">
      {%- liquid
        assign rendered_ids = ''
        assign shown = 0
      -%}
      {%- for variant in card_product.variants -%}
        {%- if variant.image == blank -%}
          {%- continue -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- assign key = variant.image.id | append: ',' -%}
        {%- unless rendered_ids contains key -%}
          {%- assign rendered_ids = rendered_ids | append: key -%}
          {%- if shown < swatch_limit -%}
            {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
            <li class="kram-card-swatches__item">
              <a
                href="{{ variant.url }}"
                class="kram-card-swatches__link"
                aria-label="{{ card_product.title | escape }} — {{ variant.title | escape }}"
              >
                <img
                  src="{{ variant.image | image_url: width: 96 }}"
                  srcset="
                    {{ variant.image | image_url: width: 48 }} 48w,
                    {{ variant.image | image_url: width: 96 }} 96w
                  "
                  sizes="48px"
                  alt=""
                  width="48"
                  height="48"
                  loading="lazy"
                >
              </a>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if overflow > 0 -%}
        <li class="kram-card-swatches__more" aria-hidden="true">+{{ overflow }}</li>
      {%- endif -%}
    </ul>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
